<%# Classroom detail, rebuilt on the shared page header.

    It hand-rolled its own h1 and actions row inside two redundant `mx-auto w-full` wrappers, with
    `my-6` on the row rather than the header block's own `mb-6`. The h1 joined three facts with
    commas - name, grade and year - so the page's accessible name carried its metadata; the name is
    the title now and the rest is the description.

    The trading switch used to sit inside the h1's flex row, which put a form control in the
    heading. It moves to the header's action area, where the page's other controls are. Its inline
    `onchange="this.form.requestSubmit()"` is a Stimulus action now - it was the last inline handler
    in the app. %>
<% content_for :title, @classroom.name %>

<div class="mx-auto w-full">
  <% meta = [
       ("Grade #{@classroom.grades_display}" if @classroom.grades_display.present?),
       @classroom.year_name
     ].compact.join(", ") %>

  <%= render layout: "components/ui/page_header",
             locals: { title: @classroom.name, description: meta } do %>
    <%= form_with url: toggle_trading_classroom_path(@classroom), method: :patch, class: "contents" do %>
      <label class="inline-flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 select-none">Trading</span>
        <%= check_box_tag "trading", "1", @classroom.trading_enabled?,
                          class: "peer sr-only",
                          disabled: !policy(@classroom).toggle_trading?,
                          data: { controller: "submit-on-change",
                                  action: "change->submit-on-change#submit" } %>
        <%# peer-checked:after:border-buffer was here and compiled to nothing - there is no
            "buffer" colour in the theme. Removed rather than guessed at. The track needs 3:1
            against the page as a UI boundary: green-700 is 4.79:1 checked, slate-400 is 2.9:1
            unchecked, so the unchecked track also carries a border. %>
        <div class="peer relative h-5 w-9 rounded-full border border-slate-400 bg-slate-300 after:absolute after:top-0.5 after:start-0.5 after:h-4 after:w-4 after:rounded-full after:bg-white after:transition-all after:content-[''] peer-checked:border-green-700 peer-checked:bg-green-700 peer-checked:after:translate-x-full rtl:peer-checked:after:-translate-x-full"></div>
      </label>
    <% end %>

    <% if @can_manage_students %>
      <%= link_to "Add student", new_classroom_student_path(@classroom), class: "tw-btn-primary" %>
      <% if policy(@classroom).edit? %>
        <%= link_to "Edit classroom", edit_classroom_path(@classroom), class: "tw-btn-secondary" %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <%# flex-col below lg. As a bare `flex` this row put the roster and the grade book list
      side by side at every width: 812px of content in a 328px viewport, which made <main>
      itself scroll sideways and carried every row action off screen with it. The pinned
      actions cell could not help, because it pins to its own table's scroll container and
      that container was the thing being pushed right. %>
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 lg:flex-row">
    <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
      <%= render "classroom_students_table", students: @classroom.users %>
    </div>

    <%# Temporary UI, to be replaced when the tabbed table is wired up. %>
    <%= render "grade_books_list", grade_books: @classroom.grade_books %>
  </div>
</div>
